ction | Description |","| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |","| `<leader>9m` | **Normal** | `select_model()` | Select from available LLM models using Telescope. |","| `<leader>9p` | **Normal** | `select_provider()` | Select from configured LLM providers (e.g. Gemini CLI, OpenCode). |","","---","","## 👷 Worker Extensions","The Worker module lets you set and track units of work within Neovim.","","| Keybinding | Mode | Function | Description |","| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |","| `<leader>9w` | **Normal** | `set_work()` | Define/set a current work item. |","| `<leader>9ws`| **Normal** | `search()` | Search and view remaining work items. |","","---","","## 💡 Pro-Tips for using `99.lua`","1. **Visual Selection Safety**: The `<leader>9v` mapping is explicitly restricted to **Visual Mode** (`v` mode) to guarantee that you only send the exact text you currently have highlighted, avoiding accidents with older or stale visual selections.","2. **Graceful Cancellations**: If you make a request that is taking too long or you want to abort, immediately hit `<leader>9x` to stop all requests and free up resources.","3. **Interactive Help**: Ready to practice? Press `<leader>9t` inside Neovim to start the official built-in interactive tutorial!"],"type":"tutorial"}},{"user_prompt":"Explain me the functionality of each keymap in @nvim/dot-config/nvim/lua/user/99.lua","data":{"qfix_items":[{"lnum":91,"text":"Visual mode keymap <leader>9v which sends the visual selection to 99 using _99.visual() for code generation or analysis","filename":"/home/mr/dotfiles/nvim/dot-config/nvim/lua/user/99.lua","col":1},{"lnum":96,"text":"Normal mode keymap <leader>9x which cancels and stops all currently active 99 generation requests using _99.stop_all_requests()","filename":"/home/mr/dotfiles/nvim/dot-config/nvim/lua/user/99.lua","col":1},{"lnum":100,"text":"Normal mode keymap <leader>9s which triggers the code search functionality of 99 using _99.search()","filename":"/home/mr/dotfiles/nvim/dot-config/n